  "question": {
    "text": "Let the set $S=\\{2,4,8,16, \\ldots, 512\\}$ be partitioned into 3 sets $A, B, C$ with equal number of elements such that $\\mathrm{A} \\cup \\mathrm{B} \\cup \\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{S}$ and $\\mathrm{A} \\cap \\mathrm{B}=\\mathrm{B} \\cap \\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{A} \\cap \\mathrm{C}=\\phi$. The maximum number of such possible partitions of $S$ is equal to:"
  },
  "options": [
